    explanation: "Pace per 100 metres is the universal language of swimming, and this calculator converts any swim into that benchmark. Enter the total distance you covered in metres and the total time it took in minutes, and it returns your pace per hundred metres, letting you compare a short set against a long continuous swim on exactly equal terms.\n\nThe metric matters because swimming distances are almost always multiples of a pool length, and coaches write sets and send-off times in seconds or minutes per hundred metres. Expressing every swim the same way lets you track conditioning across sessions, set realistic interval targets, and pace a long swim evenly instead of fading. Triathletes in particular rely on it to judge whether their race-day swim pace is sustainable before committing to it in open water.\n\nThe calculation spreads your total time across your total distance and rescales it to a hundred-metre reference, which is why it works for any swim length you enter. A falling pace per hundred metres at the same effort is clear evidence your swimming is improving, making this one of the cleanest ways to measure progress in the water. Whether you swim in a pool or open water, knowing your pace per hundred turns a distance and a stopwatch reading into a meaningful, comparable figure you can build training around.",
